RelayDesk @CMAKE_PROJECT_VERSION@ for macOS
============================================

Bundle identifier: @RELAYDESK_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER@
Package signature variant: @RELAYDESK_MACOS_PACKAGE_VARIANT@

Install
-------
Drag @CMAKE_PROJECT_PROPER_NAME@.app to Applications. Internal ad-hoc builds
are not notarized and macOS may require Control-click > Open on first launch.
Do not remove quarantine attributes manually.

Upgrade
-------
Quit RelayDesk and replace the existing app in Applications. Keep the same
bundle identifier and install path so macOS can associate existing privacy
permissions with the upgraded application. macOS may still request renewed
Accessibility, Input Monitoring, or Local Network permission after an update.

Uninstall and retained data
---------------------------
Removing @CMAKE_PROJECT_PROPER_NAME@.app does not remove settings, trusted
devices, transfer history, resumable partial-transfer state, logs, or received
files. RelayDesk user settings are stored outside the app bundle under the
user Library (the primary settings directory is ~/Library/RelayDesk), and
received files remain in the selected destination such as Downloads/RelayDesk.

Delete retained data only through an explicit RelayDesk reset/cleanup action or
by following a separately reviewed manual cleanup procedure. Package uninstall
and upgrade steps never delete user files automatically.
